WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.544
Chapter eleven: glossary.

00:00:01.544 --> 00:00:08.059
This chapter gives short meanings for the words that Scholium uses, in groups that belong together.

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:15.669
A record is a signed statement that Scholium stores, for example a paper version, a review, a consent or a decision.

00:00:15.669 --> 00:00:19.211
A version is one signed, permanent edition of a paper.

00:00:19.211 --> 00:00:22.432
Each new version links to the previous one.

00:00:22.432 --> 00:00:25.249
A sch ID is the permanent ID of a paper.

00:00:25.249 --> 00:00:28.841
A version adds its number, for example slash v two.

00:00:28.841 --> 00:00:32.411
The last characters of the ID are a checksum.

00:00:32.411 --> 00:00:35.455
Your DID is your public identifier on Scholium.

00:00:35.455 --> 00:00:40.064
It starts with did colon key, and it comes from your signing key.

00:00:40.064 --> 00:00:47.113
A passkey is the sign-in on your device, for example Face ID, Touch ID, Windows Hello or a security key.

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:50.021
The passkey unlocks your signing key.

00:00:50.021 --> 00:00:53.994
Your ORCID iD is your researcher identifier from orcid dot org.

00:00:53.994 --> 00:00:58.997
When you link it, you move to tier one, and you can recover your account.

00:00:58.997 --> 00:01:03.272
Your tier is your trust level, from zero, Reader, to four, Moderator.

00:01:03.272 --> 00:01:04.944
It decides what you can do.

00:01:04.944 --> 00:01:10.953
An endorsement is a signed statement by an experienced member that you may publish in a category.

00:01:10.953 --> 00:01:14.821
Your first endorsement makes you an Author, at tier two.

00:01:14.821 --> 00:01:19.735
A guardian is one of the five people who can approve the recovery of your account.

00:01:19.735 --> 00:01:22.112
A recovery needs three approvals.

00:01:22.112 --> 00:01:26.874
Consent is the signed agreement of each listed author to appear on a version.

00:01:26.874 --> 00:01:30.275
A version is not published until every author consents.

00:01:30.275 --> 00:01:36.549
A CRediT role is a standard description of the contribution of an author, for example Software.

00:01:36.549 --> 00:01:43.613
Listed means that a moderator accepted the paper into the public catalogue: the feed, search and the category pages.

00:01:43.613 --> 00:01:49.920
A hold is a moderation decision that keeps a version out of the listing until a problem is fixed.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.501
A policy clause is one of the published moderation rules.

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:56.264
There are ten, and every decision cites one.

00:01:56.264 --> 00:02:01.101
An appeal asks a panel of three peers to look again at a moderation decision.

00:02:01.101 --> 00:02:03.888
You can appeal once for each decision.

00:02:03.888 --> 00:02:09.652
To flag or report is to tell the moderators that a paper or post may break the policies.

00:02:09.652 --> 00:02:18.240
A tombstone is what remains after a legal takedown: the record that the content existed and was removed, without the content.

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:20.773
A formal review is a structured review.

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:28.965
It has six rubric scores with justifications, a confidence and a recommendation, and it decides the status of the paper.

00:02:28.965 --> 00:02:38.624
The rubric is the six review dimensions: soundness of method, evidence for claims, reproducibility, novelty, clarity, and limitations and ethics.

00:02:38.624 --> 00:02:44.735
To commit a review is to sign and seal it, so that nobody can read it until it is revealed.

00:02:44.735 --> 00:02:50.843
Reveal publishes a committed review, after a second reviewer commits or 21 days pass.

00:02:50.843 --> 00:02:54.790
Escrow keeps your identity as an anonymous reviewer encrypted.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:59.328
Only the integrity committee could open it, in a misconduct case.

00:02:59.328 --> 00:03:05.275
The AI pre-review is the advisory report that AI agents write after a version is listed.

00:03:05.275 --> 00:03:09.342
Discussion is open, informal comments on a paper by members.

00:03:09.342 --> 00:03:15.036
It never changes status. An annotation is a comment on one paragraph of one version.

00:03:15.036 --> 00:03:18.283
Press the A key on a paragraph to add one.

00:03:18.283 --> 00:03:24.418
The status of a paper is Preprint, Under review, Reviewed, Contested, Corrected or Retracted.

00:03:24.418 --> 00:03:27.386
A fixed rule computes it from signed records.

00:03:27.386 --> 00:03:34.448
Contested means that a reviewer judged the paper fundamentally flawed, or a moderator put it on hold.

00:03:34.448 --> 00:03:38.009
A correction is a signed notice that points out an error.

00:03:38.009 --> 00:03:42.506
It changes the status to Corrected, and shows a banner on every version.

00:03:42.506 --> 00:03:46.816
A retraction is a signed notice that nobody should rely on the paper.

00:03:46.816 --> 00:03:50.464
It changes the status to Retracted on every version.

00:03:50.464 --> 00:03:55.383
A withdrawal is a signed notice that the authors no longer stand behind a paper.

00:03:55.383 --> 00:03:57.627
It does not change the status.

00:03:57.627 --> 00:04:03.723
Verified means that your browser checked the signatures, the history and the files, and they all match.

00:04:03.723 --> 00:04:08.611
An anchor is a public timestamp that proves a record existed at a given time.

00:04:08.611 --> 00:04:12.293
The plan is to write it to a public blockchain every hour.

00:04:12.293 --> 00:04:17.200
It is not enabled in this release, so every paper shows anchor pending.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.972
An archive is a car file that you download.

00:04:19.972 --> 00:04:27.773
It holds the signed records and files of a paper, or the whole public record of the server, and you can check it offline.

00:04:27.773 --> 00:04:32.363
A node is one Scholium server, and its network page describes it.

00:04:32.363 --> 00:04:37.089
In short: a record is a signed statement, and a version never changes.

00:04:37.089 --> 00:04:41.883
A formal review decides the status, and the AI pre-review only advises.

00:04:41.883 --> 00:04:45.051
This is the end of the Scholium handbook.
